---
layout: base
---

<article>
  {% set postNumber = collections.publicWeeknotes | getPostNumber(page) %}
  {% set postVersion = page.inputPath | postVersion %}
  {# Publish date from git history, like the colophon; front-matter date is
     the fallback for drafts and uncommitted files. Set before the
     supergraphic, which shows the same date in its own format. #}
  {% set headerDate = date %}
  {% if postVersion and postVersion.published %}
    {% set headerDate = postVersion.published %}
  {% endif %}
  {#- Supergraphic: the week number over the date, set huge, cropped by the
     left edge of the viewport and stopping at its centre. It used to be a
     pure flourish, hidden from the accessibility tree because a small meta
     line below carried the same two facts as real text. That line is gone, so
     this is now the only place the week number appears at all — it stays in
     the tree and reads before the title, which is the order it would have had.
     Still not selectable: what a sighted reader sees is cropped type, and a
     selection over it would be nonsense.

     Only week notes have a number, and without one there is nothing to set. -#}
  {% if postNumber %}
  <p class="supergraphic">
    {#- Zero-padded, which with tabular figures makes this line measure the
       same on every post, so the left crop lands on the same letter
       throughout instead of drifting between one- and two-digit weeks. -#}
    <span>Week note {% if postNumber < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ postNumber }}</span>
    <span>{{ headerDate | dateNumeric }}</span>
  </p>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="post-header">
    <h1 class="page-title">{{ title }}</h1>
    {% if description %}
      <p class="post-description">{{ description }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  <hr>
  <div class="post-content">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </div>
  <hr>
  {% if postVersion %}
    <div class="post-colophon">
      <h2 class="post-colophon-label">Colophon</h2>
      <dl class="colophon-list">
      <dt>Version</dt>
      <dd>{{ postVersion.version }}{% if postVersion.draft %} (draft){% endif %}</dd>
      {% if postVersion.published %}
        <dt>Published</dt>
        <dd><time datetime="{{ postVersion.published | isoDate }}">{{ postVersion.published | dateTimeFormat }}</time></dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if postVersion.updated %}
        <dt>Last updated</dt>
        <dd><time datetime="{{ postVersion.updated | isoDate }}">{{ postVersion.updated | dateTimeFormat }}</time></dd>
      {% endif %}
      {#- Substituted after the build by src/_11ty/page-weight.js, which can
         only weigh this document once it has been written. -#}
      <dt>Weight</dt>
      <dd>@@PAGE_WEIGHT_KB@@ kB</dd>
      <dt>Words</dt>
      <dd>{{ content | wordCount }}</dd>
      <dt>Colour</dt>
      <dd>{{ page.fileSlug | postColor }}</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</article>
